- $(10) \times (1)$: This corresponds to $n = p_1^9 p_2$
- $(5) \times (3)$: This corresponds to $n = p_1^4 p_2^2$
- $(4) \times (2) \times (1)$: This corresponds to $n = p_1^3 p_2 p_3$

